# Pairs with EventualConvergence in ReplicationCausalDelivery. A writer can
# record a write it never received - here, one that was never authored - and
# then stamp a dependency on it. The receiver parks the dependent write for a
# dependency that will never arrive. Production stamps a frontier from what
# the author actually applied; this mutation shows the property is sensitive
# to that.
MODULE: EventualConvergenceDependencyOnUnseenWrite
TARGET: EventualConvergence
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: a writer learns a write that was never authored and depends on it, so the receiver waits for ever
PERTURBS: Learn

--- FIND
Learn(x, w) ==
    /\ w \in authored
--- REPLACE
Learn(x, w) ==
\* MUTATION: a write is learned whether or not it was ever authored.
    /\ w \in Writes
--- END
